{
 "section": "CRS-03",
 "name": "xeddsa-verify",
 "description": "XEdDSA signatures as deployed: 64 bytes R || s, with the Edwards sign bit of the signer carried in bit 7 of byte 63. Signatures were produced by the oracle with internal randomness, so they are verification vectors only. valid is the oracle verification result. ed25519_public_key is the birational conversion of the u-coordinate with the carried sign bit, and ed25519_standard_verify is the result of verifying ed25519_signature (byte 63 bit 7 cleared) with an independent standard Ed25519 verifier. Cases labeled s-plus-group-order replace s by s + q (still below 2^253): the oracle accepts them, while a strict RFC 8032 verifier rejects them.",
